<title>USA: U.S. April PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. April PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Apr    Mar    Apr97/96</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods    -2.6   -3.4     -1.3</p>
<p> -Gasoline		    -4.1   -4.0     -4.1</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		  1.4   -9.9    -14.2</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	 -3.3   -4.8	1.8</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Apr    Mar    Apr97/96</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods    -2.0   -4.6     -2.5</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z     -5.3  -20.7	2.0</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		    -6.1   -8.7     -7.6</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		 -0.3  -10.7    -12.6</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	   -7.2  -20.4    -11.2</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Apr    Mar    Apr97/96</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials   -5.2  -19.2     -9.9</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			 5.2    3.2	7.5</p>
<p> -Natural Gas-Z	    -13.3  -29.2    -13.3</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		 -0.4  -13.4    -15.0</p>
<p>Note-Crude energy materials include crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
